          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Tool names mix conventions: 2 snake_case, 1 camelCase. The odd ones out are `doStuff`.\n\nRename `doStuff` to snake_case so the whole server reads as one API. Mixed conventions make a tool list look assembled rather than designed, and give a model one more axis of variation that carries no meaning."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "mcpDoctorFinding/v1": "dc69f216dd467dd8"
          },
          "ruleId": "MCP004"
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "search_users",
                  "kind": "function",
                  "name": "search_users"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`search_users` promises `user` in its name, but the description never mentions it.\n\nSay what `user` means here in the first sentence of `search_users`'s description. Retrieval matches a user's phrasing against the description as much as the name, so a description that never names its own subject loses to any sibling whose description does."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "mcpDoctorFinding/v1": "a888ece65b70b9bf"
          },
          "ruleId": "MCP003"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "search_users",
                  "kind": "function",
                  "name": "search_users"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`search_users` and `search_orgs` share 78% of their meaningful words -- their descriptions are near-identical.\n\nRewrite one of them around what makes it different. If `search_users` and `search_orgs` really do the same thing, delete one; if they do not, the first sentence of each should name the thing only that one handles. Two descriptions this close are a coin flip at selection time, and the model has no way to know it guessed wrong."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "mcpDoctorFinding/v1": "16d8eee1757125d2"
          },
          "ruleId": "MCP013"
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "search_users",
                  "kind": "function",
                  "name": "search_users"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`search_users` overlaps with `search_orgs`, and its description never says which to prefer.\n\nAdd a sentence to `search_users` of the form \"Use this when X. If you need Y, use `search_orgs` instead.\" Overlap between sibling tools is normal and usually unavoidable; what separates a server whose tools get picked correctly from one whose tools do not is whether the descriptions say how to choose."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "mcpDoctorFinding/v1": "664f185df24e3012"
          },
          "ruleId": "MCP014"
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "search_users.query",
                  "kind": "parameter",
                  "name": "query"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`search_users.query` has no description.\n\nDescribe what `query` is for, what a valid value looks like, and what happens when it is omitted. An auto-generated `title` is not a description -- it is the parameter name with a capital letter."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "mcpDoctorFinding/v1": "3275d49a7923d988"
          },
          "ruleId": "MCP020"
        },
        {
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "search_users",
                  "kind": "function",
                  "name": "search_users"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Nothing in `search_users`'s schema shows an example value.\n\nPut one concrete value in the description of the least obvious parameter -- \"e.g. 'usr_1a2b'\" -- or add JSON Schema `examples`. Identifiers and formatted strings are the ones that matter: a model can guess what a search query looks like, and cannot guess what your IDs look like."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "mcpDoctorFinding/v1": "13549bf40803b35f"
          },
          "ruleId": "MCP025"
        },
        {
